HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The mmrrssaass driver first appeared in FreeBSD 10.1.

     mmffii DDrriivveerr:: mfi(4) is the old FreeBSD driver which started with support
     for Gen-1 Controllers and was extended to support up to MR-Fusion (Device
     ID = 0x005B, 0x005D, 0x005F).

     mmrrssaass DDrriivveerr:: mmrrssaass is the new driver reworked by LSI which supports
     Thunderbolt and onward products.  The SAS+SATA RAID controller with de‐
     vice id 0x005b is referred to as the Thunderbolt controller throughout
     this man page.

     ccaamm aawwaarree HHBBAA ddrriivveerrss:: FreeBSD has a cam(4) layer which attaches storage
     devices and provides a common access mechanism to storage controllers and
     attached devices.  The mmrrssaass driver is cam(4) aware and devices associ‐
     ated with mmrrssaass can be seen using camcontrol(8).  The mfi(4) driver does
     not understand the cam(4) layer and it directly associates storage disks
     to the block layer.

     TThhuunnddeerrbboolltt CCoonnttrroolllleerr:: This is the 6Gb/s MegaRAID HBA card which has de‐
     vice id 0x005B.

     IInnvvaaddeerr CCoonnttrroolllleerr:: This is 12Gb/s MegaRAID HBA card which has device id
     0x005D.

     FFuurryy CCoonnttrroolllleerr:: This is the 12Gb/s MegaRAID HBA card which has device id
     0x005F.

